title: contest_destabilized
---

Narrator:
It doesn't look like much from the outside.

It never does.

---

Narrator:
Supply disruptions.
Administrative delays.
Contradictory orders that somehow all trace back to valid sources.

---

Narrator:
The system's governance is softer now.

The local population doesn't know why.

Most of them will assume it's always been this way.

---

Narrator:
That is the point.

---

Narrator:
You don't need to own something to unsettle it.

You just need patience.

---

Narrator:
And the right kind of quiet.

---

-> [Acknowledge]
    <<jump contest_done>>

===

title: contest_failed
---

Narrator:
The pressure didn't hold.

---

Narrator:
That's the clinical summary.

The operational reality is somewhat messier.

---

Narrator:
Your agents were too visible.
Or the timing was wrong.
Or whoever runs that system is better at reading disruption than most.

---

Narrator:
No escalation.

No counter-operation.

They cleaned up the noise and moved on.

---

Narrator:
Which means they noticed.

---

Narrator:
Whether they identified the source is a different question.

One you'd rather not answer right now.

---

-> [Acknowledge]
    <<jump contest_done>>

===

title: contest_done
---
